  ## Generalized linear models (GLMs)
  \large
  \uncover<1->{Benefits of generalized linear models:}
  %[]
    * <2-> The residuals don't have to be normally distributed.
    * <3-> The response variable can be binary, integer,
      strictly-positive, etc...
    * <4-> The variance is not assumed to be constant.
    * <5-> Useful for manipulative experiments or observational
      studies, just like linear models.
  
  \vfill
  \uncover<6->{
  {Examples}
  
    * Presence-absence studies
    * Studies of survival
    * Seed germination studies
  
  }




