  ## Binomial Distribution
  {Properties}
  
    * The expected value of $y$ is $Np$
    * The variance is $Np(1-p)$
  
  \pause
  \vfill
  {Bernoulli distribution}
  
    * The Bernoulli distribution is a binomial distribution with a
      single trial ($N=1$)
%    * Think of it as a single coin flip
    * Logistic regression is usually done in this context, such
      that the response variable is 0/1 or No/Yes or Bad/Good, etc$\dots$
  



